,"_score_rev_volatility":4.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":-0.0601064187736886,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.48776540553659287,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":18.7,"_gate_incr_roic":0.01721050489163048,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":22.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.46447911635527883,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09299820579346196,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":71.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.37134651091294524,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04577463430630828,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":62.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.019946882143971,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":74.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012795414305424786,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00802,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Kite Realty Group Trust is a real estate investment trust (REIT) that owns and operates a high-quality portfolio of open-air shopping centers and mixed-use destinations. The Company's portfolio is concentrated in high-growth Sun Belt and select strategic gateway markets. KRG has more than six decades of experience in developing, operating, and investing in real estate, using a disciplined, hands-on approach to enhance portfolio quality and maximize long-term value for all stakeholders. As of September 30, 2026, the Company owned interests in 164 U.S. open-air shopping centers and mixed-use assets, comprising approximately 26.3 million square feet of gross leasable space. Kite Realty Group Trust was incorporated in 1971 in Maryland and based in Indianapolis.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John A. Kite | Chairman of the Board of Trustees & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 228 people. Revenue per employee of $3.7M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.2M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $47K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Kite Realty Group Trust is a mid-cap real estate business with a $5.2B market cap on $844M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $278M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.44\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 28% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2781859898677619},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Financial quality scores above most Real Estate peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kite Realty Group Trust (NYSE:KRG) Cut to \u201cNeutral\u201d at Bank of America","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/kite-realty-group-trust-nysekrg-cut-to-neutral-at-bank-of-america.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572472.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (KRG) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_KRG_Volatility_111226065402_1794484442.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794484442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"compan